The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```
/* in gether_disconnect() – old code */
...
usb_ep_disable(link->in_ep);
... /* free requests, clear in_ep->desc */
usb_ep_disable(link->out_ep);
... /* free requests, clear out_ep->desc */
spin_lock(&dev->lock);
dev->port_usb = NULL;   /* cleared too late */
link->is_suspend = false;
spin_unlock(&dev->lock);
```
Reason:
The clearing of `dev->port_usb` is delayed until after the endpoints are disabled and their descriptors cleared. During this window, a concurrent `eth_stop()` can see `dev->port_usb` as non‑NULL, call `usb_ep_enable()` with already‑disabled descriptor pointers, and cause a NULL pointer dereference.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
/* in gether_disconnect() – fixed code */
spin_lock(&dev->lock);
dev->port_usb = NULL;
link->is_suspend = false;
spin_unlock(&dev->lock);

netif_stop_queue(dev->net);
netif_carrier_off(dev->net);
... /* then disable endpoints */
```
Reason:
By moving the assignment of `dev->port_usb = NULL` (and the suspend flag) to the very beginning of `gether_disconnect()`, any concurrent `eth_stop()` will see a NULL pointer and safely bail out before touching the endpoints. This eliminates the race window and prevents the NULL dereference.

